_refine.details                                  
;THE YEAST CCP USED HERE IS A RECOMBINANT [CALLED CCP(MI)
AND EXPRESSED IN E. COLI] WHICH HAS A MET-ILE DIPEPTIDE
FUSED TO THE N-TERMINUS.  THIS MET-ILE DIPEPTIDE WAS NOT
INCLUDED IN THIS STRUCTURE DUE TO DISORDER.

THERE WAS UNEXPLAINED ELECTRON DENSITY ABOVE THE HEME IRON
INTO WHICH WATER MOLECULES ALONE COULD NOT BE MODELED.  AN
SO- GROUP, A POSSIBLE DEGRADATION PRODUCT OF DTT, WAS
PLACED HERE AND WAS TREATED AS AN INCOMPLETE SULFATE ION
DURING REFINEMENT.  THIS IS NOT A SULFATE ION.  IT IS ONLY
CALLED A SULFATE ION FOR SIMPLICITY.
;
